Package: aggregateR
Title: Aggregate Loss Distributions from R through 'aggregate-api'
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Stephen J.", "Mildenhall", , "steve@convexrisk.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A thin client for 'aggregate-api', the HTTP service in front
    of the 'aggregate' actuarial library for compound (aggregate) loss
    distributions. Write a program in the library's DecL language, build
    it on a server, and read its exhibits, quantiles and whole frames as
    data frames. Talks to the public server or to a private local one.
License: BSD_3_clause + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/mynl/aggregate-R
BugReports: https://github.com/mynl/aggregate-R/issues
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    httr2,
    jsonlite,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-US
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
